= Inductive bias — Simple =

An '''inductive bias''' is an assumption or preference that helps a learning system decide what pattern to learn from limited data.

For example, a system might prefer simpler rules, nearby examples, smooth functions, or patterns that stay the same after certain transformations.

Inductive bias is not automatically a mistake.

A good bias can help a system generalize.

A bad match between the bias and the task can hurt performance.

